### Running the daemon

One of the important things to note about RabbitMQ is that it stores data based on what it calls the "Node Name", which defaults to the hostname. If you want to use a hostname other than the one provided by AppJail, you can configure a custom one in an `appjail-template(5)` file.

```console
$ cp /usr/local/share/appjail/files/default_template.conf template.conf
$ chmod +w template.conf
$ appjail-config set -t template.conf host.hostname=my-rabbit
$ appjail oci run -Pd \
    -o overwrite=force \
    -o virtualnet=":<random> default" \
    -o nat \
    -o template=template.conf \
    ghcr.io/appjail-makejails/rabbitmq some-rabbit
...
[00:00:33] [ info  ] [some-rabbit] Detached: pid:76709, log:jails/some-rabbit/container/2026-08-11.log
```

This will start a RabbitMQ container listening on the default port of 5672. If you give that a minute, then do `appjail logs read jails/some-rabbit/container/2026-08-11.log`, you'll see in the output a block similar to:

```
  Starting broker...2026-08-11 18:50:14.834947-04:00 [info] <0.208.0>
2026-08-11 18:50:14.834947-04:00 [info] <0.208.0>  node           : rabbit@my-rabbit
2026-08-11 18:50:14.834947-04:00 [info] <0.208.0>  home dir       : /var/db/rabbitmq
2026-08-11 18:50:14.834947-04:00 [info] <0.208.0>  config file(s) : /usr/local/etc/rabbitmq/conf.d/10-defaults.conf
2026-08-11 18:50:14.834947-04:00 [info] <0.208.0>                 : /usr/local/etc/rabbitmq/conf.d/20-management_agent.disable_metrics_colle
ctor.conf
2026-08-11 18:50:14.834947-04:00 [info] <0.208.0>  log(s)         : <stdout>
2026-08-11 18:50:14.834947-04:00 [info] <0.208.0>  data dir       : /var/db/rabbitmq/mnesia/rabbit@my-rabbit
```

Note the `data dir` there, especially that it has my "Node Name" appended to the end for the file storage. This image makes all of `/var/db/rabbitmq` a volume by default.

